{# Labelled group of link rows. Dispatches each link on its `kind`: the report
   row for `report`, the plain row otherwise — the seam a later kind renderer
   plugs into with one new branch in the dispatch below (D6). Both rows were
   components of their own until D7 folded them in here: `link-group` was their
   only caller, so the boundary bought nothing and cost two directories, two
   contracts and three stories that could drift from the group that dispatches
   them. The `rows` slot is a composition escape hatch and WINS over the `links`
   prop when filled. Renders nothing when it has neither, because a group with a
   promising label and no rows is worse than an absent one.

   EMPTINESS IS TESTED WITH `is not empty`, NOT WITH BARE TRUTHINESS. A group
   whose kinds match no link is handed `links: []` by the mapping, and the two
   engines that render this template disagree about that value: PHP Twig reads
   an empty array as false, while the Storybook renderer is JavaScript, where
   `[]` is truthy. Written `{% if links %}` the guard therefore held in Drupal
   and silently failed on the review surface — three groups printed their
   headings with nothing under them, which is exactly the "promising label and
   no rows" this component exists to avoid (C3, D4).

   THE ROWS BUILD THEIR ATTRIBUTES WITH A BARE `create_attribute()`, not with
   `attributes ?: create_attribute()`. As components they were included with
   `with_context = false` and only the link's own props, so `attributes` was
   never defined inside them and the fallback always won. Inlined, `attributes`
   IS in scope — it is the group's — and `attributes ?:` would stamp the whole
   group's attributes onto every single row.

   THE PASSED-COUNT GUARD GAINED `is defined`, and that is not cosmetic. As a
   component the report row wrote `{% if passed is not null %}`, which is the
   right test there: an omitted prop is an UNDEFINED VARIABLE, and an undefined
   variable is null. Inlined, the same value is a MISSING HASH KEY (`link.passed`
   on a link that carries no count), and the Storybook renderer's Twig — which is
   JavaScript — reads that as `undefined`, which `is not null` reports as TRUE.
   Copied across unchanged, the guard therefore emitted a stray `<span> passed
   </span>` for every countless report link. `is defined` restores the component
   behaviour exactly; the rendered markup of both kinds is byte-identical to the
   two components' across every kind, every count and both slot paths. #}
{% set icon_map = {
  mr: 'merge-request',
  branch: 'branch',
  ci: 'pipeline',
  report: 'report',
  ddev: 'play',
  design: 'palette',
  doc: 'link'
} %}
{% if rows or links is not empty %}
  <div{{ (attributes ?: create_attribute()).addClass(['link-group', 'flex', 'flex-col', 'gap-[5px]']) }}>
    {% if label %}
      <div class="link-group__label text-eyebrow font-semibold text-text-faint uppercase tracking-[0.04em]">{{ label }}</div>
    {% endif %}
    <div class="link-group__rows flex flex-col gap-[3px]">
      {% block rows %}
        {% if rows %}
          {{ rows }}
        {% else %}
          {% for link in links %}
            {% if (link.kind|default('doc')) == 'report' %}
              {# The report row: the plain row plus its pass/fail counts and
                 duration. It renders only its own props and fetches nothing —
                 a real artifact reader is a follow-up backend ticket (D6),
                 because the GitLab credentials it would need live on the
                 conductor's machine rather than on the control plane. The icon
                 comes from the sprite through the icon component, same as the
                 plain row — never an inlined SVG path. #}
              <div{{ create_attribute().addClass(['link-report-row', 'flex', 'items-center', 'gap-[6px]', 'min-w-0']) }}>
                {{ include('bb_theme:icon', { name: icon_map[link.kind]|default('link'), size: 'sm' }, with_context = false) }}
                {% set new_tab = link.target|default('_blank') != '_self' %}
                <a class="link-report-row__title min-w-0 overflow-hidden text-ellipsis whitespace-nowrap text-caption text-text no-underline hover:underline" href="{{ link.url }}"{% if new_tab %} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"{% endif %}>{{ link.title|default(link.url) }}{% if new_tab %}<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span>{% endif %}</a>
                <span class="flex-1"></span>
                <span class="link-report-row__counts flex items-center gap-[8px] shrink-0">
                  {% if link.passed is defined and link.passed is not null %}<span class="text-caption font-mono tabular-nums text-state-running">{{ link.passed }} passed</span>{% endif %}
                  {% if link.failed %}<span class="text-caption font-mono tabular-nums text-state-attention">{{ link.failed }} failed</span>{% endif %}
                  {% if link.duration %}<span class="text-caption font-mono tabular-nums text-text-faint">{{ link.duration }}</span>{% endif %}
                </span>
              </div>
            {% else %}
              {# One typed link: a kind icon (from the sprite, via the icon
                 component — never an inlined SVG path) plus an external anchor.
                 Unknown kind falls back to the doc icon (link symbol). Long
                 titles truncate rather than wrap or push the row wider. #}
              <div{{ create_attribute().addClass(['link-row', 'flex', 'items-center', 'gap-[6px]', 'min-w-0']) }}>
                {{ include('bb_theme:icon', { name: icon_map[link.kind]|default('link'), size: 'sm' }, with_context = false) }}
                {% set new_tab = link.target|default('_blank') != '_self' %}
                <a class="link-row__title min-w-0 overflow-hidden text-ellipsis whitespace-nowrap text-caption text-text no-underline hover:underline" href="{{ link.url }}"{% if new_tab %} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"{% endif %}>{{ link.title|default(link.url) }}{% if new_tab %}<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span>{% endif %}</a>
              </div>
            {% endif %}
          {% endfor %}
        {% endif %}
      {% endblock %}
    </div>
  </div>
{% endif %}
